# Quant Platform Rules

This repository is a portfolio-risk, regime-detection, stress-testing,
backtesting, and research platform. It is **not** a stock-prediction app.

## Framing

- Do not claim reliable alpha, market prediction, guaranteed risk reduction, or
  investment performance.
- Keep language conservative and research-oriented.
- Do not produce buy/sell instructions or personalized financial advice.

## Data and leakage safety

- Preserve `pandas.DatetimeIndex` on every time-series output.
- Use trailing or expanding windows only. Never use centered rolling windows.
- Split chronologically into train / validation / test before any learned fit.
- Fit scalers and models on the training period only; transform/infer afterward.
- Backtests must separate signal, decision, execution, and return dates.
- No same-close execution and no look-ahead from future information.
- Prefer deterministic random seeds for stochastic models.

## Architecture

- Single package: `mrrp` under `src/`. Do not create a second package.
- Keep financial math in reusable typed modules.
- Keep Streamlit pages thin; no duplicated calculations in pages or notebooks.
- Drive research parameters through YAML configs.
- Dashboard tests must use temporary fixtures or injected paths, never ignored
  developer-local artifacts or live network calls.

## Validation commands

- `make setup`
- `make data`
- `make dashboard`
- `make features`
- `make feature-check`
- `make models` / `make model-check` (when present)
- `make stress` (when present)
- `make backtest` (when present)
- `make report` (when present)
- `make test`
- `make lint`
- `make check`
- `make format`
- `make clean`

## Process

- Inspect before editing.
- Add tests for every new financial/feature/model/stress/backtest function.
- Run `make check` before considering work complete.
- Do not push, merge, force-push, rewrite history, or tag releases without
  explicit approval.
- Do not add dependencies without explicit approval.
